IMPORT prelude

-- Mutual Benefit Organisations Act 1960 (Singapore) -- what counts as a mutual benefit organisation (s 2), the duty to register
-- and the exemptions (ss 4(1), 37, 48), when the Registrar must or may refuse registration (s 6), which decisions go on appeal to
-- the Minister (ss 7, 9(3), 28(6), 34(5), 36(1)), who may not act as an officer (s 12), minors as members (s 17), whom a member may
-- nominate for benefits (s 18), paying a death benefit (s 22(4)), special resolutions (ss 25, 26), members' applications for an
-- inspector or a dissolution investigation (ss 27(1), 34(1)), notice before cancellation or suspension (s 28(2), (3)), the
-- penalties (ss 12(2), 29(3), 30(2), 38, 39, 40, 42(2), 44, 45, 46) and whose property answers a judgment (s 47(3)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/MBOA1960.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021", and is headed
-- "Informal Consolidation -- version in force from 1/11/2024". The latest amendment annotated in the body is [Act 30 of 2024 wef
-- 01/11/2024] (s 48(1), adding the Platform Workers Act 2024). The meta file records the version as current at 1 October 2026.
-- The arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is out of step with the body from s 32 on; the body's numbers are used.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0146 (subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl): Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. SCOPED to what a member, an officer, a nominee or an organiser meets. Not encoded: the Registrar's appointment
-- (s 3), the application papers and certificate (ss 4(2)-(4), 5), the annual Gazette list (s 8), the registered office, trustees'
-- appointment, audit, annual return and balance-sheet duties (ss 10, 11(1)-(3), 13, 14, 15) except as they feed s 42, the priority
-- on an officer's death or bankruptcy (s 16), the members' copy and inspection rights (ss 19, 20, 21), the reserve-fund
-- and bank-account rules (ss 22(1)-(3), 23), change of name (s 24), the inspector's powers (s 27(2)-(6)), the cancellation grounds
-- as such (s 28(1)) and its effects (s 28(4), (5)), the freezing and seizure powers (ss 29(1), (2), 30(1)), winding up (s 31),
-- dissolution procedure (ss 32, 33, 34(2)-(7), 35), dispute procedure (s 36(2)-(4)), presumptions (s 41), vicarious liability
-- (s 43), service (s 47(1), (2)), the Minister's exemptions as a discretion (s 48(2)), the rule-making power (s 49) and the
-- Schedule. No rules made under s 49 (fees, the s 22(1) administration percentage) were retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions as shown in the example rows. No
-- pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Mutual Benefit Organisations Act 1960 -- organisations`

§§ `2 -- what a mutual benefit organisation is`

-- s 2: "mutual benefit organisation" means any organisation which by its objects and rules "either as the principal object or as
-- an ancillary object makes provision by voluntary subscriptions of the members thereof or subscribers thereto with or without the
-- aid of donations" for (a) relief or maintenance of members, subscribers or listed relatives "during sickness or other infirmity
-- ... in old age or in widowhood", or of orphan children during minority; (b) "the payment of money on the birth of a member's or
-- subscriber's child or on the death of a member or subscriber" or listed relatives "or on the death of any other person or for
-- the funeral expenses"; or (c) relief or maintenance "when unemployed or when in distressed circumstances".
DECLARE Object IS ONE OF
    `relief in sickness or infirmity`
    `maintenance in old age`
    `relief of widows`
    `maintenance of orphans`
    `a payment on the birth of a child`
    `a payment on a death`
    `funeral expenses`
    `relief when unemployed`
    `relief in distressed circumstances`
    `holidays and outings`
    `investment returns`

GIVEN `the object` IS AN Object
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the object is a benefit object` IF
    CONSIDER `the object`
    WHEN `holidays and outings` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `investment returns` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- "Either as the principal object or as an ancillary object": a club whose benefit scheme is a side line is still caught.
GIVEN `the object` IS AN Object, `funded by voluntary subscriptions of members or subscribers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a mutual benefit organisation` IF
    `the object is a benefit object` `the object` AND `funded by voluntary subscriptions of members or subscribers`

§§ `4(1), 37, 48(1) -- registration, unlawful organisations and the exemptions`

-- s 4(1): "Every mutual benefit organisation shall apply for registration under this Act."
-- s 37: "Every mutual benefit organisation, not being a registered organisation, shall be deemed to be an unlawful organisation."
-- s 48(1): "Nothing in this Act shall apply to any person, body or organisation to which the Insurance Act 1966 applies or which is
-- registered under the Co-operative Societies Act 1979, the Trade Unions Act 1940 or the Platform Workers Act 2024." (2) the
-- Minister may exempt.
GIVEN `it is an MBO` IS A BOOLEAN, `registered under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Insurance Act 1966 applies to it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `registered as a co-operative, trade union or under the Platform Workers Act 2024` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `exempted by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an unlawful organisation` IF
        `it is an MBO`
    AND (NOT `registered under this Act`)
    AND (NOT `the Insurance Act 1966 applies to it`)
    AND (NOT `registered as a co-operative, trade union or under the Platform Workers Act 2024`)
    AND (NOT `exempted by the Minister`)

§§ `6 -- refusal of registration`

-- s 6(1): the Registrar "shall refuse" if satisfied that (a) the rules are insufficient for proper management and control; (b) it
-- is likely to be used for unlawful purposes or purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order; (c) an officer or
-- manager "is not of good character"; (d) the scheme is undesirable and not in members' interest; (e) "the total number of members
-- thereof or subscribers thereto is less than 50"; (f) the application does not comply; (g) the rules and objects are contrary to
-- the Act; or (h) registration would be contrary to the public interest.
-- (2): the Registrar "may refuse" if (a) the name is identical with or so nearly resembles another's "as is likely to deceive",
-- or is likely to mislead; or (b) "no satisfactory evidence has been produced of the good character" of the officers.
-- Grounds (b), (d), (f), (g), (h) of s 6(1) are folded into one flag here.
GIVEN `members and subscribers` IS A NUMBER, `the rules are insufficient` IS A BOOLEAN, `an officer is not of good character` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `another s 6(1) ground is made out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar must refuse registration` IF
        `members and subscribers` LESS THAN 50
    OR  `the rules are insufficient`
    OR  `an officer is not of good character`
    OR  `another s 6(1) ground is made out`

GIVEN `the name is deceptively similar or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN, `satisfactory evidence of officers' character was produced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may refuse registration` IF
    `the name is deceptively similar or misleading` OR (NOT `satisfactory evidence of officers' character was produced`)

§§ `7, 9(3), 28(6), 34(5), 36(1) -- what can be appealed to the Minister`

-- s 7: a person aggrieved by a decision under s 5(1) or (5) or s 6 may, "within one month of being notified", appeal to the
-- Minister "whose decision shall be final". s 9(3): refusal to register an amendment of rules -- appeal to the Minister. s 28(6):
-- cancellation or suspension -- appeal to the Minister. s 34(5): a dissolution order after investigation is "final and conclusive
-- ... without appeal". s 36(1): a dispute decided under the rules is "binding and conclusive on all parties without appeal, and
-- shall not be removable to any court or restrainable by injunction".
DECLARE Decision IS ONE OF
    `refusal of registration`
    `conditions imposed on registration`
    `refusal to register an amendment of the rules`
    `cancellation or suspension of registration`
    `a dissolution order after investigation`
    `a dispute decided under the rules`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision may be appealed to the Minister` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `a dissolution order after investigation` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a dispute decided under the rules` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `12 -- who may not act as an officer`

-- s 12(1): no person shall act as an officer or manage or assist in management if "(a) he has been convicted of any offence
-- involving dishonesty or moral turpitude and has not received a free pardon; or (b) he has been convicted of any other offence and
-- sentenced to a fine of not less than $2,000 or to imprisonment for a term of not less than one year and has not received a free
-- pardon, unless the written permission of the Minister so to act is first obtained." (2): $500 or 6 months or both.
-- The words "unless the written permission of the Minister ..." are printed inside para (b). Read literally, they qualify (b)
-- only, so the Minister cannot lift the bar in (a). That is the reading encoded; it is flagged in NOTES.md.
GIVEN `convicted of an offence of dishonesty or moral turpitude` IS A BOOLEAN, `fine imposed in dollars` IS A NUMBER,
      `imprisonment imposed in months` IS A NUMBER, `received a free pardon` IS A BOOLEAN, `has the Minister's written permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is barred from acting as an officer` IF
        (NOT `received a free pardon`)
    AND (    `convicted of an offence of dishonesty or moral turpitude`
         OR  ((`fine imposed in dollars` AT LEAST 2000 OR `imprisonment imposed in months` AT LEAST 12)
              AND (NOT `has the Minister's written permission`)))

§§ `17 -- minors as members`

-- s 17(1): the rules "may provide for the admission of a person under 21 years of age as a member or subscriber". (2): such a
-- member "may, if he is over 16 years of age, by himself and if he is under that age by his parent or guardian, execute all
-- instruments and give all acquittances", "but shall not be a member of the committee, or a trustee, secretary, manager or
-- treasurer". Ages are whole years here; "over 16" is read as more than 16 (an inference for a person aged exactly 16).
DECLARE Post IS ONE OF
    `ordinary member`
    `committee member`
    `trustee`
    `secretary`
    `manager`
    `treasurer`

GIVEN `age in years` IS A NUMBER, `the post` IS A Post
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may hold the post` IF
        `age in years` AT LEAST 21
    OR  `the post` EQUALS `ordinary member`

GIVEN `age in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the minor signs for himself` IF
    `age in years` GREATER THAN 16

§§ `18 -- whom a member may nominate`

-- s 18: no member may nominate to receive benefits a person other than "the wife, children (including adopted children),
-- grandchildren, mother, father, sons-in-law, daughters-in-law, brothers or sisters of the whole blood, brothers or sisters of the
-- half-blood, children of such brothers and sisters of the whole or half-blood, uncles or aunts of the whole blood, uncles or aunts
-- of the half-blood or children of those uncles or aunts". Proviso: a member "may nominate any other person in writing signed by
-- himself in the presence of and attested by a Justice of the Peace or a Magistrate or the Registrar".
-- The list says "wife", not "husband" or "spouse", and has no grandparents.
DECLARE Relation IS ONE OF
    `wife`
    `husband`
    `adopted child`
    `grandchild`
    `half-brother`
    `nephew or niece`
    `first cousin`
    `grandparent`
    `uncle by marriage`
    `friend`

GIVEN `the nominee` IS A Relation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the nominee is in the s 18 list` IF
    CONSIDER `the nominee`
    WHEN `husband` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `grandparent` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `uncle by marriage` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `friend` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the nominee` IS A Relation, `signed before a JP, Magistrate or the Registrar who attested it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the nomination is valid` IF
    `the nominee is in the s 18 list` `the nominee` OR `signed before a JP, Magistrate or the Registrar who attested it`

§§ `22(4) -- paying a death benefit`

-- s 22(4): no payment on a death "except upon the production of the original death certificate or a certified copy thereof"
-- (or, for a death abroad, the foreign authority's certificate). Proviso: "payment may be made to the personal representative of a
-- deceased member or subscriber where no nomination has been made upon the production of letters of administration or probate".
GIVEN `a death certificate or certified copy was produced` IS A BOOLEAN, `a nomination was made` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `paid to the personal representative on production of probate or letters of administration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the death benefit may be paid` IF
        `a death certificate or certified copy was produced`
    OR  ((NOT `a nomination was made`) AND `paid to the personal representative on production of probate or letters of administration`)

§§ `25, 26 -- special resolutions`

-- s 25(1): a special resolution is one (a) "passed by a majority of not less than three-fourths" of members entitled to vote and
-- present at a general meeting of which notice of the intention was duly given; and (b) "confirmed by a majority" of those
-- present at a subsequent general meeting "held not less than 14 days nor more than one month from the day of the meeting at which
-- the resolution was first passed". s 26: a signed copy is sent to the Registrar "and until that copy is registered the special
-- resolution shall not take effect". "Not more than one month" is taken as a flag, to avoid turning a month into days.
GIVEN `votes for at the first meeting` IS A NUMBER, `voters present at the first meeting` IS A NUMBER, `days between the meetings` IS A NUMBER,
      `the second meeting was within one month of the first` IS A BOOLEAN, `votes for at the second meeting` IS A NUMBER,
      `voters present at the second meeting` IS A NUMBER, `registered by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the special resolution takes effect` IF
        (`votes for at the first meeting` TIMES 4) AT LEAST (`voters present at the first meeting` TIMES 3)
    AND `days between the meetings` AT LEAST 14
    AND `the second meeting was within one month of the first`
    AND (`votes for at the second meeting` TIMES 2) GREATER THAN `voters present at the second meeting`
    AND `registered by the Registrar`

§§ `27(1), 34(1) -- members asking the Registrar to step in`

-- s 27(1): "Upon the application of one-fifth of the total number of members", the Registrar may appoint an inspector or call a
-- special meeting. s 34(1): on the written application of "one-fifth of the total number of members", the Registrar may investigate
-- with a view to dissolution, on "not less than one month's previous notice in writing to the organisation".
GIVEN `members applying` IS A NUMBER, `total members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `enough members have applied` IF
    (`members applying` TIMES 5) AT LEAST `total members`

§§ `28(2), (3) -- notice before cancellation or suspension`

-- s 28(3): unless the Registrar has given "not less than 2 months previous notice in writing specifying briefly the ground", the
-- registration "shall not be cancelled (except at its request) or suspended". (2): a suspension is for "any term not exceeding
-- 3 months", renewable for the like period.
GIVEN `at the organisation's request` IS A BOOLEAN, `months of written notice given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may cancel now` IF
    `at the organisation's request` OR `months of written notice given` AT LEAST 2

GIVEN `months of written notice given` IS A NUMBER, `months of suspension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the suspension is within the Registrar's power` IF
    `months of written notice given` AT LEAST 2 AND `months of suspension` AT MOST 3

§§ `Penalties -- ss 12(2), 29(3), 30(2), 38, 39, 40, 42(2), 44, 45, 46`

-- s 12(2) acting while barred: $500 or 6 months. s 29(3) bank manager ignoring a freezing order: $3,000 or 3 years. s 30(2)
-- obstructing seizure of records: $2,000 or 3 years. s 38 office-bearer or manager of an unlawful organisation: $3,000 or 3 years.
-- s 39 "is or acts as a member of an unlawful organisation or attends a meeting": $1,000 or one year. s 40 "knowingly allows a
-- meeting" of an unlawful organisation on premises: $1,000 or one year. s 42(2) failures to give notices, returns, information:
-- "a fine not exceeding $200" -- no imprisonment. s 45(1) false rules, (2) misappropriation: $500 or 6 months. s 46 falsifying a
-- balance sheet or return: $500 or 6 months.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `s 12 acting as an officer while barred`
    `s 29 bank manager disobeying a freezing order`
    `s 30 obstructing seizure of records`
    `s 38 running an unlawful organisation`
    `s 39 being a member of or attending an unlawful organisation`
    `s 40 allowing an unlawful organisation to meet on premises`
    `s 42 failing to give a notice, return or information`
    `s 45 misappropriating property`
    `s 46 falsifying a return`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 29 bank manager disobeying a freezing order` THEN 3000
    WHEN `s 38 running an unlawful organisation` THEN 3000
    WHEN `s 30 obstructing seizure of records` THEN 2000
    WHEN `s 39 being a member of or attending an unlawful organisation` THEN 1000
    WHEN `s 40 allowing an unlawful organisation to meet on premises` THEN 1000
    WHEN `s 42 failing to give a notice, return or information` THEN 200
    OTHERWISE 500

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 29 bank manager disobeying a freezing order` THEN 36
    WHEN `s 30 obstructing seizure of records` THEN 36
    WHEN `s 38 running an unlawful organisation` THEN 36
    WHEN `s 39 being a member of or attending an unlawful organisation` THEN 12
    WHEN `s 40 allowing an unlawful organisation to meet on premises` THEN 12
    WHEN `s 42 failing to give a notice, return or information` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE 6

-- s 44: "Every default under this Act constituting an offence, if continued, shall constitute a new offence in every week during
-- which the default continues." Counting one offence for each week the default runs is an inference about how the weeks are
-- counted; the text does not say whether the first week is the original offence or a new one.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `weeks the default runs` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum total fine for a continuing default` MEANS
    `the maximum fine` `the offence` TIMES `weeks the default runs`

§§ `47(3) -- whose property answers a judgment`

-- s 47(3): "The judgment in any suit against a registered organisation shall not be enforced against the person or property of any
-- officer or member of the organisation but only against the property of the organisation."
DECLARE Target IS ONE OF
    `the organisation's property`
    `an officer's property`
    `a member's property`

GIVEN `the target` IS A Target
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the judgment may be enforced against` IF
    `the target` EQUALS `the organisation's property`
